\pard\cf1\b\f2\fs32 Free Security Check Tools for Windows\f0\b0\fs22\cf0\par
\pard\fs20\i A friendly guide to check if your PC has a problem - all tools are free.\i0\fs22\par
\par
\cf1\b\f1 1. Full Antivirus / Malware Scanners (get a second opinion)\f0\b0\cf0\par
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/wdsi/threats/scanner"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 Microsoft Safety Scanner}}}  - on-demand, single-use scan (official Microsoft).
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.malwarebytes.com"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 Malwarebytes Free}}}  - excellent second-opinion scanner and adware remover.
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://usa.kaspersky.com/downloads/free-virus-removal-tool"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 Kaspersky Virus Removal Tool}}}  - free portable virus remover.
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eset.com/us/online-scanner/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 ESET Online Scanner}}}  - one-time online scan, no install.
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hitmanpro.com"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 HitmanPro}}}  - fast cloud second-opinion scanner.
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sophos.com/en-us/products/free-tools/virus-removal-tool"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 Sophos Virus Removal Tool}}}  - removes active or blocked threats.
\par
\cf1\b\f1 2. Rootkit / Stealth Threat Scanners\f0\b0\cf0\par
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.malwarebytes.com/adwcleaner"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 Malwarebytes AdwCleaner}}}  - removes adware and unwanted programs.
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gmer.net"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 GMER}}}  - rootkit and process inspector (advanced users).
\par
\cf1\b\f1 3. System Inspection (see what is running and auto-starting)\f0\b0\cf0\par
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 Sysinternals Suite (Microsoft)}}}  - free official tools.
     - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/process-explorer"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 Process Explorer}}}  - see every running process.
     - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/autoruns"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 Autoruns}}}  - see everything that starts at boot/login.
     - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/tcpview"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 TCPView}}}  - see all network connections.
     - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/procmon"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 Process Monitor}}}  - watch files/registry/network live.
\par
\cf1\b\f1 4. Network / Firewall Monitoring\f0\b0\cf0\par
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.glasswire.com"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 GlassWire Free}}}  - visual network traffic monitor.
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wireshark.org"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 Wireshark}}}  - deep packet inspection (advanced).
\par
\cf1\b\f1 5. Ransomware Help\f0\b0\cf0\par
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nomoreransom.org"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 No More Ransom}}}  - free decryptors for many ransomware strains.
\par
\cf1\b\f1 6. Account / Browser Checks (no install needed)\f0\b0\cf0\par
 - Microsoft account: Security > Sign-in activity - see recent logins and locations.
 - Outlook / OneDrive: check for unknown sign-ins or shares.
 - Browser: check Extensions and Saved passwords; remove anything you do not remember.
 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://haveibeenpwned.com"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf1 Have I Been Pwned}}}  - check if your email was in a data breach.
\par
\cf1\b\f1 7. When to Run These\f0\b0\cf0\par
 - Monthly, or when suspicious: Malwarebytes Free + a full Windows Defender scan.
 - PC acting weird: Windows Defender Offline scan + Malwarebytes + Autoruns/Process Explorer.
 - After clicking something risky: run the Microsoft Safety Scanner and Kaspersky KVRT, then change your passwords.
\par
\cf1\b\f1 Red Flags (run a scan if you see these)\f0\b0\cf0\par
 - Sudden slowness, or high CPU/disk with nothing open.
 - New toolbars/extensions, changed homepage, random pop-ups.
 - Browser redirects, unknown processes, unexpected accounts or logins.
 - Files renamed with .locked or .crypt (ransomware).
\par
\cf1\b\f1 If You Think You Are Infected\f0\b0\cf0\par
 1. Disconnect from the internet.
 2. Run a Windows Defender Offline scan and one second-opinion scanner.
 3. Change important passwords from another device.
 4. Check Microsoft account sign-in activity; sign out other sessions.
 5. Consider System Restore (from the System Optimizer tool) or restore from a backup.
\par
